01-shared-ui — finite branch-trust audit packet 1. Scope, authority, and required disposition This lane owns exactly 87 changed paths. The attached package stat is 14,460 insertions and 3,219 deletions, with the heaviest churn in semantic collection, shared components, popup lifecycle, row metrics, design contracts, and the consistency explorer. attachment-0002-ce2f86fc8fb9e99… attachment-0003-114ab44d3670a24… The PackX bundle is useful for identifying high-risk seams, but it contains only 11 repository files. It cannot establish complete package coverage; the worker must inspect the actual main...HEAD diff for all 87 owned paths. attachment-0001-c72c26427701003… The audit must enforce these rules: Shared components and theme/chrome tokens are the source of truth. New surface-local values or a third row/state/input system are presumptive defects unless explicitly justified. Cargo always runs through ./scripts/agentic/agent-cargo.sh. Source-reading tests are architectural decision locks, not ordinary behavior coverage. The locked glass values, fixtures, envelopes, and thresholds are immutable in this campaign. A visual, keyboard, focus, lifecycle, or temporal claim is not verified until it crosses the corresponding real boundary. attachment-0001-c72c26427701003… +2 The explorer is evidence about intended contracts, not product proof. Its own README says source-derived browser projections are not native screenshots and do not prove GPUI/AppKit pixels, focus, accessibility, glass, or runtime behavior. attachment-0001-c72c26427701003… Allowed finding classes CodeMeaningMinimum evidenceVIVerified improvementDiff trace to live consumer plus passing focused proof; native proof when the claim is visual, focus, lifecycle, or temporalVRVerified regressionReproduction with observed wrong output plus source owner and failing proofPRPlausible regressionConcrete source contradiction and executable scenario, but no completed reproductionUCUnproven AI claimDocs, comments, manifest, or test names claim behavior without sufficient boundary proofNRNo material regression foundDiff inspected, consumers traced, relevant proof passesNANon-production or generated-only changeProven generated, vendored, or review-only with no hidden product effect Confidence suffix -H: source, consumer, focused test, and required runtime boundary agree. -M: source and behavior test agree; native runtime was unnecessary or unavailable. -L: static evidence only. -U: explicitly unverified. Do not write “fixed,” “safe,” “consistent,” “complete,” or “runtime-confirmed” without meeting those levels. 2. Exact first implementation action Run this from the repository root. The manager-provided attachment names are the defaults; alternate materialized locations may be supplied through the two environment variables. Bashset -euo pipefail set -o pipefail LANE=".notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/01-shared-ui" INPUT_CHANGED_PATHS="${INPUT_CHANGED_PATHS:-changed-paths.txt}" INPUT_DIFF_STAT="${INPUT_DIFF_STAT:-diff-stat.txt}" mkdir -p \ "$LANE/inputs" \ "$LANE/receipts" \ "$LANE/diffs" \ "$LANE/snippets" \ "$LANE/sandbox" \ "$LANE/tmp" test -f "$INPUT_CHANGED_PATHS" test -f "$INPUT_DIFF_STAT" cp "$INPUT_CHANGED_PATHS" "$LANE/inputs/changed-paths.txt" cp "$INPUT_DIFF_STAT" "$LANE/inputs/diff-stat.txt" printf '%s %s\n' \ 'ce2f86fc8fb9e993ecec23c38a6b5e1f628e8364ac6a90b65a7c0aad8a2b2eca' \ "$LANE/inputs/changed-paths.txt" \ | shasum -a 256 -c - printf '%s %s\n' \ '114ab44d3670a24e461afd974c1c6f297401c5f25a1ac5e0b40a86250726f45a' \ "$LANE/inputs/diff-stat.txt" \ | shasum -a 256 -c - BRANCH="$(git branch --show-current)" START_HEAD="$(git rev-parse HEAD)" START_MAIN="$(git rev-parse main)" START_MERGE_BASE="$(git merge-base main HEAD)" COMMIT_COUNT="$(git rev-list --count main..HEAD)" BRANCH_PATH_COUNT="$(git diff --name-only main...HEAD | wc -l | tr -d ' ')" test "$BRANCH" = "consistency/default-recommendations" test "$COMMIT_COUNT" -eq 50 test "$BRANCH_PATH_COUNT" -eq 481 LC_ALL=C sort -u "$LANE/inputs/changed-paths.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-paths.sorted.txt" test "$(wc -l < "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-paths.sorted.txt" | tr -d ' ')" -eq 87 test -z "$(LC_ALL=C sort "$LANE/inputs/changed-paths.txt" | uniq -d)" git diff --name-only main...HEAD | LC_ALL=C sort -u \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-all-branch-paths.sorted.txt" comm -23 \ "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-paths.sorted.txt" \ "$LANE/receipts/00-all-branch-paths.sorted.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-paths-missing-from-diff.txt" test ! -s "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-paths-missing-from-diff.txt" xargs git diff --name-status main...HEAD -- \ < "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-paths.sorted.txt" \ | tee "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-name-status.tsv" xargs git diff --numstat main...HEAD -- \ < "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-paths.sorted.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-numstat.tsv" read -r PACKAGE_ADDED PACKAGE_DELETED <<EOF $(awk ' $1 ~ /^[0-9]+$/ { added += $1 } $2 ~ /^[0-9]+$/ { deleted += $2 } END { print added + 0, deleted + 0 } ' "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-numstat.tsv") EOF test "$PACKAGE_ADDED" -eq 14460 test "$PACKAGE_DELETED" -eq 3219 git status --porcelain=v1 \ | grep -vF "$LANE/" \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-production-status-before.txt" || true set +e xargs git diff --check main...HEAD -- \ < "$LANE/receipts/00-owned-paths.sorted.txt" \ > "$LANE/receipts/00-diff-check.txt" 2>&1 DIFF_CHECK_RC=$? set -e cat > "$LANE/receipts/00-refs.env" <<EOF BRANCH=$BRANCH START_HEAD=$START_HEAD START_MAIN=$START_MAIN START_MERGE_BASE=$START_MERGE_BASE COMMIT_COUNT=$COMMIT_COUNT BRANCH_PATH_COUNT=$BRANCH_PATH_COUNT PACKAGE_PATH_COUNT=87 PACKAGE_ADDED=$PACKAGE_ADDED PACKAGE_DELETED=$PACKAGE_DELETED DIFF_CHECK_RC=$DIFF_CHECK_RC EOF This immediately proves or falsifies branch identity, attachment identity, branch size, package ownership, and package churn. Exact first audit-artifact write Immediately after the command above, write: Bashsource "$LANE/receipts/00-refs.env" cat > "$LANE/00-inventory.md" <<EOF # 01-shared-ui inventory and accounting ## Candidate identity - Branch: \`$BRANCH\` - HEAD: \`$START_HEAD\` - main: \`$START_MAIN\` - merge-base: \`$START_MERGE_BASE\` - main..HEAD commits: $COMMIT_COUNT - complete branch paths: $BRANCH_PATH_COUNT ## Package accounting - Expected owned paths: 87 - Accounted owned paths: 87 - Insertions: $PACKAGE_ADDED - Deletions: $PACKAGE_DELETED - Ownership input SHA-256: \`ce2f86fc8fb9e993ecec23c38a6b5e1f628e8364ac6a90b65a7c0aad8a2b2eca\` - Diff-stat input SHA-256: \`114ab44d3670a24e461afd974c1c6f297401c5f25a1ac5e0b40a86250726f45a\` - Diff-check exit: $DIFF_CHECK_RC - Missing owned paths: \`receipts/00-owned-paths-missing-from-diff.txt\` ## Subsystem partition | Subsystem | Path count | |---|---:| | Consistency explorer and manifest | 20 | | Generated tokens, design contract, theme definitions | 11 | | Layout model and semantic collectors | 5 | | Rows, sections, list chrome, launcher rendering | 13 | | Inputs, forms, buttons, shortcuts, prompt shells | 19 | | Inline popup lifecycle | 1 | | Semantic states, conversations, Notes, toasts | 14 | | Vendored gpui-component changes | 4 | | **Total** | **87** | ## Evidence precedence 1. Actual \`main...HEAD\` bytes and current call sites 2. Compiler and behavior tests 3. Real runtime receipts from one target generation 4. Static screenshots and browser projections 5. Design explorer, prior ledgers, comments, and PackX excerpts ## Current package state \`OPEN\` — completion requires 87 path-ledger rows, classified findings, terminal receipts, screenshot requests, integration hunks, ranked next actions, and proof that no production bytes were changed. EOF 3. Required lane artifact structure The worker must create only these audit artifacts and receipts: .notes/oracle/branch-trust-audit/lanes/01-shared-ui/ ├── 00-inventory.md ├── 01-path-ledger.tsv ├── 02-observed-improvements.md ├── 03-breakage-candidates.md ├── 04-proof-gaps.md ├── 05-verification.md ├── 06-screenshot-requests.md ├── 07-article-hunks.md ├── 08-next-actions.md ├── worker-report.md ├── inputs/ │ ├── changed-paths.txt │ └── diff-stat.txt ├── diffs/ │ ├── 00-owned-full.patch │ └── 01-*.patch through 08-*.patch ├── receipts/ │ ├── 00-refs.env │ ├── 00-owned-name-status.tsv │ ├── 00-owned-numstat.tsv │ ├── 00-production-status-before.txt │ ├── 00-production-status-after.txt │ ├── 01-*.txt through 08-*.txt │ └── verification-summary.tsv ├── snippets/ │ └── finding-specific source excerpts ├── sandbox/ │ └── isolated generator/export runs only └── tmp/ No production file, shared article source, integrated ledger, root manifest, generated output, commit, branch, or deployment may be changed. 01-path-ledger.tsv schema The file must have exactly 88 lines: one header and 87 unique paths. path subsystem change_kind added deleted symbols_reviewed intended_claim live_consumers tests_reviewed proof_level disposition confidence finding_ids evidence_paths screenshot_ids notes Allowed disposition values: VerifiedImprovement VerifiedRegression PlausibleRegression UnprovenClaim NoMaterialRegression GeneratedParityOnly VendorRisk Blocked No row may retain TODO, Unknown, or an empty disposition at package completion. Finding-entry structure Every entry in 02-observed-improvements.md, 03-breakage-candidates.md, or 04-proof-gaps.md must contain: Markdown## UIA-F-### — <title> - Class: VI | VR | PR | UC - Severity: P0 | P1 | P2 | P3 - Confidence: High | Medium | Low | Unverified - Files: - Symbols: - Commit lineage: - Claimed behavior: - Input/state: - Observed output: - Expected contract: - User impact: - Static evidence: - Behavior proof: - Runtime proof: - Screenshot relevance: - What this evidence does not prove: - Future remediation: - Article-ready sentence: For a PR, Observed output must say Not reproduced; it must not silently describe an expected failure as an observation. 4. Shared capture helpers Define these once for all work packages: Bashrun_timed() { python3 - "$@" <<'PY' import subprocess import sys seconds = int(sys.argv[1]