\ design/consistency/groups/context-identity.html \ design/consistency/groups/conversations-flow.html \ design/consistency/groups/cues-actions.html \ design/consistency/groups/dictation.html \ design/consistency/groups/geometry-settings.html \ design/consistency/groups/governance-contracts.html \ design/consistency/groups/inputs-popups.html \ design/consistency/groups/notes-today.html \ design/consistency/groups/proof-truth.html \ design/consistency/groups/rows-sections.html \ design/consistency/groups/states-recovery.html \ design/consistency/index.html \ design/consistency/shared/explorer.css \ design/consistency/shared/explorer.js \ design/consistency/tests/browser-smoke.mjs \ design/consistency/tests/validate-explorer.mjs \ design/consistency/tools-build-data.py Inspect these exact data anchors and behaviors: schemaVersion, truthLabels, groupCount, taskCount, groups, tasks, and taskRecords. All local-storage read/write/reset/export sites. Current/proposal/reference/negative labels. Group-page ID resolution and URL routing. Fixture paths and whether missing fixtures fail closed. Decision export ordering and whether unset decisions remain distinguishable from approval. Generator input source, output destination, normalization, ordering, and failure handling. Browser smoke assertions: distinguish page-loaded checks from actual task, label, fixture, decision, and export assertions. CSS separation between product fragments using --sk-* and explorer-only chrome using --cx-*. The manifest itself demands privacy-safe receipts, exhaustive quality-graded projection, and model/paint parity. Those statements are audit targets, not evidence that the branch achieved them. attachment-0001-c72c26427701003… Falsifiable scenarios Duplicate one task ID in a lane-only copy of groups.json → validator must fail nonzero. Change groupCount to 11 in a lane-only copy → validator must fail. Delete one group HTML file in a lane-only copy → validator or smoke test must fail. Mark a proposal