ce read protects behavior expressible by type, pure resolver, GPUI test, or runtime probe. Owners: owning component test module. Change: Replace source-string assertion with the highest available enforcement rung. Proof: New behavior test fails against the negative control and passes current code; source-audit inventory shrinks or stays flat. Non-goals: Do not delete genuinely load-bearing architectural locks without replacement. Stop: No new ordinary behavior depends solely on formatted source text. UI-NEXT-07 — isolate or upstream vendored component behavior Priority: P2 Trigger: Vendor patch affects unrelated consumers, lacks a regression test, or has no rationale/upstream record. Owners: gpui-component vendor patch and Script Kit wrapper owner. Change: Prefer a local adapter when behavior is Script Kit-specific; otherwise retain a minimal tested vendor patch with upstream lineage. Proof: Vendor package tests plus Script Kit wrapper/component runtime checks. Non-goals: No vendor framework replacement. Stop: Exact behavior owner, regression test, and patch lineage are recorded. 11. One-pass failure policy For each failed check: Preserve the first receipt unchanged. Perform at most one diagnosis pass. Correct only an invocation, lane-owned fixture, local server setup, or proven environmental interference. Rerun once. If the second run fails, times out, or cannot establish one target generation, record VR, PR, UC, or Blocked and stop that proof branch. Special cases: INVALID_INTERFERENCE from a glass probe permits one quiet-input rerun. It is never a green result. A zero-test Cargo filter is a failed proof, even with exit 0. A moving HEAD, moving main, or changed merge-base invalidates all candidate-bound receipts. Do not repair production in this campaign. Do not weaken assertions, raise tolerances, change expected screenshots, or update generated outputs to make tests pass. 12. Completion and stop checks Before writing worker-report.md, run: Bashsource "$LANE/rece